  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "If an item is sold for \\(x\\) dollars, there is a loss of \\(15\\%\\) based on the cost. If, however, the same item is sold for \\(y\\) dollars, there is a profit of \\(15\\%\\) based on the cost. The ratio \\(y:x\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(23:17\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(17y:23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(23x:17\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "dependent upon the cost"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "none of these"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "23/17"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1969-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the cost is \\(C,\\) then \\(x=0.85C\\) and \\(y=1.15C.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} y:x&=1.15C:0.85C\\\\ &=115:85=23:17. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Let the cost be \\(C\\)",
        "Write \\(x=0.85C\\) and \\(y=1.15C,\\) then form the ratio"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
